🖥️ TERMINAL-WISE PROCEDURE

This is the most important part for your lab exam.

Terminal 1 — Start Kafka
docker ps

If containers are stopped:

docker start zookeeper
docker start kafka

Then:

docker exec -it kafka bash

Create topic:

bin/kafka-topics.sh --create --topic quickstart-events --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

Describe:

bin/kafka-topics.sh --describe --topic quickstart-events --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

Start producer:

bin/kafka-console-producer.sh --topic quickstart-events --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

Type:

Hello Kafka
First Message
Second Message

Do not close Terminal 1.

Terminal 2 — Consumer

Open a new terminal.

docker exec -it kafka bash

Then:

bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh --topic quickstart-events --from-beginning --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

Output:

Hello Kafka
First Message
Second Message
🛑 How to Stop

When your experiment is complete:

Stop producer

Press:

Ctrl + C
Stop consumer

Press:

Ctrl + C
Exit Kafka container
exit
Stop Kafka and ZooKeeper

From normal Ubuntu terminal:

docker stop kafka zookeeper
⚠️ COMMON PROBLEM: Topic Already Exists

If you run:

bin/kafka-topics.sh --create --topic quickstart-events --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

and get:

Topic 'quickstart-events' already exists

Don't worry.

The topic has already been created.

Simply continue with:

bin/kafka-topics.sh --describe --topic quickstart-events --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

Then start the producer.

⚠️ COMMON PROBLEM: Container Already Exists

If you get:

Conflict. The container name "/kafka" is already in use

Don't run docker run again.

Use:

docker start kafka

and:

docker start zookeeper
